& [Intent]
  + give a hashed reentry packet a small executable integrity surface without letting self-consistency masquerade as authority

& [Work]
  + preserved source and completed SJS review and phase lock before implementation
  + implemented domain-separated request and frame commitments over three disjoint envelope shapes
  + separated self-contained local validation from reconstruction against validated canonical custody
  + projected and strictly serialized the full deterministic Slice6C fixture as ordered envelopes
  + tested corrupt packets locally coherent substitutions reordered packets and mutated canonical projection

& [Observation]
  + hash checking lowers the cost of detecting transport corruption but cannot answer who produced a packet or whether it belongs to this run
  + canonical reconstruction supplies the missing identity relation without copying the whole retained history into each packet
  + this is the implementable primitive behind hashing a frame before reentry

& [FacultyAttribution]
  + Honesty separated integrity binding authentication semantic truth and execution claims
  + Security domain-separated hashes and rejected illegal optional-field combinations
  + Planner fixed phase kind index and ordered-set structure
  + Weaver linked compact envelopes to their retained-prefix commitment
  + Scribe made all packet identities and denials inspectable in strict JSON
  + Refiner kept the local check small and left full replay in host custody
  + Observer required both local and canonical tests before acceptance

& [Next]
  + publish Slice6D and refreshed regression evidence
  + model dispatch and receipt as effectless states before any live-provider activation
